Sources for `frontend-design` skill (see plans/skill-audits/frontend-design.md for full audit):

- Vercel `frontend-design` plugin (installed globally as `frontend-design:frontend-design`) — https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-skills — vendored with void-harness additions (mobile-first dual-quality, matrix integration, shadcn composition)
- citypaul/.dotfiles UI patterns — density, hierarchy notes
- Refactoring UI (Adam Wathan + Steve Schoger) — book — foundation, density, hierarchy, motion principles
- Apple HIG visual design chapter — https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines — mobile layout heuristics
- Folpe DESIGN.md convention (per-project) — brand identity belongs in consumer DESIGN.md
- pbakaus/impeccable-design — referenced by citypaul
- impeccable (standalone skill) — VENDORED (DEV-389, build-time half): the current-AI-tell absolute bans (side-stripe, gradient-text, glassmorphism, hero-metric, eyebrow/numbered-markers, cream/sand body, text-overflow), the color-strategy commitment axis, and the type/layout/motion/interaction specifics. Its audit/critique/refine half went to the new `harness:ui-review`; its browser runtime is deferred to Vague 4.
- gstack /design-review — the Krug reading model (scan/satisfice/muddle) vendored here (DEV-389); its designer's-eye QA went to ui-review.

Strategy: vendor-plugin + distill. Fork Vercel plugin for the void-harness invariant (mobile-first dual-quality) + matrix integration; DEV-389 enriched it with impeccable's build-time craft so the harness is self-contained on UI (no external impeccable dependency).

Companion hooks: viewport-screenshot-gate (shared with accessibility), anti-ai-slop-grep.

Stack-specific @repo/ui + design system tokens + Tailwind config in pack-nextjs-pwa.

DEV-444 adaptation: consumes a fresh-context Experience Designer brief before build; independent
post-build judgment remains downstream in ui-review and Visual Craft Director.
